schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: "ERC-721 (Non-Fungible Token Standard)"
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    An Ethereum token standard, launched in 2018, in which every token is
    unique and individually identified within its contract — used for
    digital art/collectibles, event tickets, ownership certificates, and
    impact tokens like carbon-removal or biodiversity credits.
  source_traditions:
    - Ethereum Improvement Proposal 721 (ERC-721), per ethereum.org documentation.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Named in the article as the standard for representing
    specific-verifiable-action impact credits (e.g. carbon removal,
    biodiversity), land/credential ownership certificates, and event tickets.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - non-fungible token (NFT)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      ERC-721 vs ERC-20: uniqueness (each token has its own ID) vs
      interchangeability.
    - >-
      ERC-721's "safe transfer" function only sends tokens to addresses
      capable of handling them — a safeguard the article contrasts with
      ERC-20's lack of that protection.
  tensions: []
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Grouping all "impact tokens" under ERC-721 risks obscuring that
    ERC-1155 can represent similar unique/semi-fungible impact assets
    within a single contract, which the article covers separately.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/token-standards.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
